# Android GitHub release tags (auto-updater)

Owner: **Nanda**. Related: `.cursor/rules/versioning.mdc`, `lib/Misc/auto_updater.dart`.

## User policy (RU intent)

«Все будущие коммиты на GitHub должны быть с новым тегом и версией, чтобы на Android всегда была авто-установка.»

## Interpretation (default)

- **Means every shipped Android build / GitHub Release that attaches an APK** — not literally every git commit.
- Pure docs / chore / rule-only commits may stay on the current `1.x.y` **without** a product tag, unless the user asks to tag that commit too.
- If a fix/feature must reach sideload Android users via the in-app GitHub updater → treat it as a **product release**.

## Required for each Android APK ship

1. Bump marketing version `1.x.y` (patch or feature line) — follow `versioning.mdc` + `keep-docs-current.mdc`.
2. Create a **new** git tag `v1.x.y` (never reuse / clobber an existing tag expecting updater pickup).
3. Publish a GitHub Release for that tag with the new APK (and IPA if shipping).

## Why

`AppUpdater` prompts only when latest release `tag_name` is **strictly newer** than installed `versionName`. Replacing the APK on the same tag (e.g. clobber `v1.5.2`) does **not** trigger auto-update.

## Do not

- Expect auto-update after `--clobber` / re-upload on the same `v1.x.y`.
- Ship user-facing Android fixes on GitHub without a new `1.x.y` + `v1.x.y`.
